effortless-ntwf:q-hr-ai-authored-commitments a effortless-ntwf:RoleQuestions ;
    effortless-ntwf:roleQuestionId "q-hr-ai-authored-commitments" ;
    effortless-ntwf:askingRole effortless-ntwf:hr-policy-owner ;
    effortless-ntwf:witnessLoop effortless-ntwf:loop-01 ;
    effortless-ntwf:questionText "kf-policy-ai-boundary says AI may draft but may not create legal commitments. policy-03 and policy-06 are both assigned to policy-drafting-agent and se-policy03 was executed by policy-drafting-ai. Is that boundary actually being held?" ;
    effortless-ntwf:whyItMatters "This is the single commitment in the whole policy procedure that I would be asked about under oath. We wrote down the rule — AI drafts, humans commit — as an Approved Explicit fragment sourced from counsel. Then we built a procedure where an AI executes drafting steps and a pipeline sends the results. Whether the human approval step actually sits between them is a structural property nobody checks. If policy-05 were ever skipped or executed by software, the boundary would be violated and the model would say nothing." ;
    effortless-ntwf:answerableBefore false ;
    effortless-ntwf:witnessedAnswer "StepExecutions.SoftwareDidHumanWork=0/12; StepExecutions.StepIsSoftwareAssigned=5/12; StepExecutions.WasExecutedBySoftware=5/12; Steps.GateHeldByHuman=2/17; Steps.IsHumanApprovalGate=2/17; Steps.IsSoftwareAssigned=8/17" ;
    effortless-ntwf:semanticTypeIri "urn:effortless:pko-extension#RoleQuestion" .

effortless-ntwf:q-hr-unapproved-knowledge-in-my-name a effortless-ntwf:RoleQuestions ;
    effortless-ntwf:roleQuestionId "q-hr-unapproved-knowledge-in-my-name" ;
    effortless-ntwf:askingRole effortless-ntwf:hr-policy-owner ;
    effortless-ntwf:witnessLoop effortless-ntwf:loop-01 ;
    effortless-ntwf:questionText "kf-policy-manager-route is Status=Reviewed and I am its OwnerRole. exc-unreachable routes real employee cases on that exact 48-hour rule. Which claims am I the owner of that were never approved?" ;
    effortless-ntwf:whyItMatters "The knowledge authority asks whether the procedure runs on unapproved knowledge. I ask a narrower and more uncomfortable version: which of those unapproved claims are mine. OwnerRole on kf-policy-manager-route is hr-policy-owner — me — and its Status is Reviewed. I own a belief that governs how we treat an unreachable employee, and I never finished approving it. That is a personal accountability question, not a governance statistic." ;
    effortless-ntwf:answerableBefore false ;
    effortless-ntwf:witnessedAnswer "KnowledgeFragments.HasOperationalReliance=2/7; KnowledgeFragments.IsAwaitingApproval=1/7; KnowledgeFragments.IsMyUnfinishedApproval=1/7; KnowledgeFragments.IsUnapprovedAndOperationallyLive=1/7; KnowledgeFragments.OwnerIsMe=1/7" ;
    effortless-ntwf:semanticTypeIri "urn:effortless:pko-extension#RoleQuestion" .

effortless-ntwf:q-hr-what-was-actually-sent a effortless-ntwf:RoleQuestions ;
    effortless-ntwf:roleQuestionId "q-hr-what-was-actually-sent" ;
    effortless-ntwf:askingRole effortless-ntwf:hr-policy-owner ;
    effortless-ntwf:witnessLoop effortless-ntwf:loop-01 ;
    effortless-ntwf:questionText "policy-07 sends approved communications under channel controls, and kf-policy-channel says disputes are resolved against the complete approved email. If an employee disputes what they received, can I show that what was sent matched what I approved?" ;
    effortless-ntwf:whyItMatters "This is the question I will actually be asked in a dispute, and it is the one this model is furthest from answering. policy-05 is where I approve meaning; policy-06 renders; policy-07 sends. Between approval and delivery sit a drafting AI and a notification pipeline, and the model records no link at all from a sent message back to the approval that authorized it. MessageTemplates and CommunicationPolicies exist as specifications; nothing records an instance." ;
    effortless-ntwf:answerableBefore false ;
    effortless-ntwf:witnessedAnswer "ProcedureExecutions.DeliveredWithoutApproval=0/2; ProcedureExecutions.HasDelivered=0/2; ProcedureExecutions.HasHumanApproval=2/2; StepExecutions.IsApprovalExecution=1/12; StepExecutions.IsVerified=12/12" ;
    effortless-ntwf:semanticTypeIri "urn:effortless:pko-extension#RoleQuestion" .

effortless-ntwf:q-hr-policy-knowledge-half-life a effortless-ntwf:RoleQuestions ;
    effortless-ntwf:roleQuestionId "q-hr-policy-knowledge-half-life" ;
    effortless-ntwf:askingRole effortless-ntwf:hr-policy-owner ;
    effortless-ntwf:witnessLoop effortless-ntwf:loop-01 ;
    effortless-ntwf:questionText "policy-v1.0.0 was issued 2026-06-01 on knowledge elicited in May from Amina, Noah and me. My stewardship promises a 60-day cadence. Is the policy I own now resting on knowledge older than the policy itself has been reviewed?" ;
    effortless-ntwf:whyItMatters "Employment policy is where stale knowledge becomes legal exposure — a jurisdictional rule that changed, a consent requirement that moved, a channel constraint that a provider silently altered. My 60-day cadence is the tightest in the model precisely because policy knowledge decays fast. But cadence governs the REVIEW; nothing governs the KNOWLEDGE. A version can be reviewed perfectly on schedule while every fragment underneath it quietly ages past usefulness, and both facts live in this model without ever meeting." ;
    effortless-ntwf:answerableBefore false ;
    effortless-ntwf:witnessedAnswer "KnowledgeFragments.ExceedsOwningCadence=7/7; KnowledgeFragments.IsAgingLowConfidenceClaim=2/7; KnowledgeFragments.IsLowConfidence=2/7; ProcedureVersions.KnowledgeIsStalerThanCadence=3/3" ;
    effortless-ntwf:semanticTypeIri "urn:effortless:pko-extension#RoleQuestion" .

effortless-ntwf:q-variance-ai-authority-provenance a effortless-ntwf:RoleQuestions ;
    effortless-ntwf:roleQuestionId "q-variance-ai-authority-provenance" ;
    effortless-ntwf:askingRole effortless-ntwf:variance-review-agent ;
    effortless-ntwf:witnessLoop effortless-ntwf:loop-01 ;
    effortless-ntwf:questionText "By what authority am I executing close-04, when did that authority begin, who approved it, and who held this role before me?" ;
    effortless-ntwf:whyItMatters "This is the question almost no enterprise can answer about its own automated controls: which of our controls are now executed by a non-human, since when, and under what approval. Everything needed is already in `RoleAssignments` as data — `ra-old-variance` and `ra-new-variance` — but it is inert. Nothing surfaces 'this role changed species', nothing names the approving authority, and nothing links the handover to a ChangeRequest. I need my own provenance as columns before I act." ;
    effortless-ntwf:answerableBefore false ;
    effortless-ntwf:witnessedAnswer "RoleAssignments.IsHumanToNonHumanHandover=1/13; RoleAssignments.IsNonHumanAssignment=4/13; RoleAssignments.IsUnauthorizedNonHumanAssignment=3/13" ;
    effortless-ntwf:semanticTypeIri "urn:effortless:pko-extension#RoleQuestion" .

effortless-ntwf:q-variance-ai-quality-vs-human-baseline a effortless-ntwf:RoleQuestions ;
    effortless-ntwf:roleQuestionId "q-variance-ai-quality-vs-human-baseline" ;
    effortless-ntwf:askingRole effortless-ntwf:variance-review-agent ;
