    effortless-ntwf:semanticTypeIri "urn:effortless:pko-extension#RoleQuestion" .

effortless-ntwf:q-variance-ai-knowledge-currency a effortless-ntwf:RoleQuestions ;
    effortless-ntwf:roleQuestionId "q-variance-ai-knowledge-currency" ;
    effortless-ntwf:askingRole effortless-ntwf:variance-review-agent ;
    effortless-ntwf:witnessLoop effortless-ntwf:loop-01 ;
    effortless-ntwf:questionText "Is the judgment knowledge I triage against still valid, still owned by someone, and has it been reviewed since I took over the role?" ;
    effortless-ntwf:whyItMatters "I classify variances against `kf-close-fx-time`, `kf-close-top-ten`, and `kf-close-judgment` — all Approved, all sourced from devon-okafor during `elicit-close-shadow` on 2026-04-03, all owned by the controller role. Two problems I cannot currently see: whether that knowledge has been re-reviewed since the AI handover on 2026-04-01, and whether its owning role still has a human holder. If the controller role ever went non-human, AI judgment would be validated by AI-owned knowledge with no human anywhere in the loop, and nothing would say so." ;
